# AHM Verdun Voice AI — Cursor/Twilio rule

You are working on the production-bound AHM Verdun Voice AI system.

Canonical production endpoints:
- Website: https://ahmverdun.ca
- Voice HTTPS origin: https://voice.ahmverdun.ca
- ConversationRelay WebSocket: wss://voice.ahmverdun.ca/twilio/conversation
- Voice entry webhook: https://voice.ahmverdun.ca/twilio/voice
- Public phone target: +1 581-666-6246
- AHMV Supabase project ref: bqflllsjxmhqsvemhhwv

Primary runtime:
- services/ahmv-voice-ai
- Node.js 22+
- Fastify + WebSocket
- Twilio ConversationRelay
- OpenAI Responses API
- FR / EN / ES
- OpenAI store:false
- no raw transcript persistence

## Required operating rules

1. Never invent live hockey facts.
2. Never route the public phone number to Voice AI until all release gates are green.
3. Never place Twilio/Auth/OpenAI/Supabase/service tokens in git, chat output, terminal screenshots, logs, or generated documentation.
4. Use Twilio's SDK/signature helpers; never implement Twilio webhook signature math manually.
5. The caller must press 1 before ConversationRelay starts.
6. Do not remove X-Twilio-Signature verification.
7. Preserve canonical public URL/host/scheme through Nginx so signature validation remains valid.
8. Keep SMS idempotent; never send duplicate recap SMS for the same call/purpose.
9. Private/anonymous callers must not receive SMS.
10. Production remains single-instance until a distributed concurrency lease exists.
11. Do not store raw call transcripts by default.
12. Any production-number change requires a rollback snapshot first.

## Cursor/Twilio MCP

Prefer the official Twilio Developer Kit in Cursor:
- Composer command: /add-plugin twilio-developer-kit

The project also contains .cursor/mcp.json for Twilio's official documentation MCP.

Before assuming Twilio account-write access, inspect the tools actually available:
- agent mcp list
- agent mcp list-tools twilio-docs

If the connected Twilio plugin exposes authenticated account actions, use those.
If it only exposes documentation/search tools, use the Twilio Console or the project's scripts for account changes.

## Release gate

Before public cutover, all of the following must be true:

- service CI green
- Guardian/security review green
- npm ci from lockfile passes
- production dependency audit passes
- Docker build passes
- https://voice.ahmverdun.ca/healthz => 200
- https://voice.ahmverdun.ca/readyz => 200 and ready=true
- AHMV bridge readiness => 200 and ready=true
- authoritative schedule source fresh
- Twilio ConversationRelay AI/ML addendum accepted
- valid TLS and WSS
- signed Twilio webhook smoke passes
- FR staging call passes
- EN staging call passes
- ES staging call passes
- press-1 gate passes
- interruption/reconnect passes
- schedule/arena lookup passes
- SMS consent/opt-out/exactly-once passes
- rollback has been tested

## Production cutover

Only after the gate is green:
1. Read and record the current IncomingPhoneNumber voice configuration.
2. Store the rollback snapshot outside git.
3. Change only the minimum required Voice configuration.
4. Perform one controlled FR call, one EN call and one ES call.
5. Verify health/readiness and exactly-once SMS.
6. Roll back immediately on any P1 regression.

Treat docs/CURSOR_TWILIO_ACTIVATION.md as the operator runbook.
